[{:db/id "6e160412-70c4-5898-9627-1e775d2346d7" :answer/id #uuid "6e160412-70c4-5898-9627-1e775d2346d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{x}{9y}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "6675c608-2d79-51da-8ce1-3d915d6d59c8" :answer/id #uuid "6675c608-2d79-51da-8ce1-3d915d6d59c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{y}{9x}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "2a5b1be4-7c6e-5722-a2f4-2aa1b2aae130" :answer/id #uuid "2a5b1be4-7c6e-5722-a2f4-2aa1b2aae130" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9x}{y}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "8c584b97-62a0-5d84-bf7d-5b2abde11f40" :answer/id #uuid "8c584b97-62a0-5d84-bf7d-5b2abde11f40" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{9x}{y}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "055f7f68-8860-5fcd-ba89-65573245d570" :answer/id #uuid "055f7f68-8860-5fcd-ba89-65573245d570" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3x}{y}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "cc377f79-c91d-5163-84d3-cf26a1ed63ab" :answer-field/id #uuid "cc377f79-c91d-5163-84d3-cf26a1ed63ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["6e160412-70c4-5898-9627-1e775d2346d7" "6675c608-2d79-51da-8ce1-3d915d6d59c8" "2a5b1be4-7c6e-5722-a2f4-2aa1b2aae130" "8c584b97-62a0-5d84-bf7d-5b2abde11f40" "055f7f68-8860-5fcd-ba89-65573245d570"] :answer-field/correct "8c584b97-62a0-5d84-bf7d-5b2abde11f40" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "d7a2ead7-a103-561d-ae19-16273e0e5510" :question/id #uuid "d7a2ead7-a103-561d-ae19-16273e0e5510" :question/problem "![](images/4e/4efe76bd06d22c5735b427c150f5a09b7288f8281b90921aeb11902c864176e5.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the ellipse shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our ellipse is centered at the origin and has semiaxes $1$ and $3,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{1}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}=1\\,⟹\\,{x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}) & =0 \\\\ 2x+\\frac{2y}{9}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2y}{9}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{9x}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["cc377f79-c91d-5163-84d3-cf26a1ed63ab"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "generator" :question-generator/id #uuid "23e3dea6-0070-5c2d-9841-01d73c2e86aa" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186166866.py"} [:db/add 17592186166866 :knowledge-point/question-generator "generator"] {:db/id 17592186166866 :knowledge-point/questions ["d7a2ead7-a103-561d-ae19-16273e0e5510"]} [:db/ensure 17592186166866 :knowledge-point/validate]]
